{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running a cobbler-scaffold \"stitch\" task (#5232) to implement `cmd/tty/main.go` - a Go reimplementation of the GNU `tty` utility. The task requires implementing srd052-tty requirements R1.1 through R2.1: printing the terminal device name when stdin is a terminal, printing \"not a tty\" when it's not, proper exit codes (0/1/2), and silent mode (-s/--silent/--quiet). The implementation must follow strict coding standards defined in the execution constitution and go_style_constitution.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - GNU coreutils `tty` utility reimplementation in Go\n   - Terminal detection via `os.Stdin.Fd()` and `sys.IsTerminal()`\n   - Terminal device name retrieval (likely via `golang.org/x/sys/unix.Ttyname()`)\n   - SIGPIPE handler installation via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Differential testing pattern against `gtty` reference binary\n   - Exit code semantics: 0 = terminal, 1 = not a terminal, 2 = error\n   - Silent mode flag (-s, --silent, --quiet) suppresses all output\n   - pkg/sys package provides `IsTerminal(fd uintptr) bool` and `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd052-tty.yaml` (READ)\n     - Contains the full SRD for the tty utility\n     - R1.1: stdin is terminal → print device name + newline, exit 0\n     - R1.2: stdin not terminal → print \"not a tty\" + newline, exit 1\n     - R1.3: -s/--silent/--quiet → suppress output, exit code only (0 or 1)\n     - R2.1: extra operands → error to stderr, exit 2\n     - R2.2: unknown flags → error to stderr, exit 2\n     - Non-goals: does not configure terminal, only checks stdin\n   \n   - `cmd/tty/main.go` (TO BE CREATED)\n     - The sole file to implement; must contain all tty logic\n     - Must start with SPDX copyright header\n     - Must call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at start of main()\n     - Must use `os.Stdin.Fd()` for terminal detection (design decision D3)\n   \n   - `pkg/sys/` (REFERENCE - from project_context source code)\n     - `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` in sigpipe.go - installs SIGPIPE handler matching GNU behavior\n     - `IsTerminal(fd uintptr) bool` - exported in contract but implementation in terminal.go (not shown in source)\n     - `FileInfo`, `Stat()`, `Lstat()` in fileinfo.go / stat_darwin.go\n     - Already imports `golang.org/x/sys/unix`\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet; implementation has not started.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Key design question: How to get the terminal device name in Go. Options considered:\n     1. `golang.org/x/sys/unix.Ttyname(0)` - most reliable, but requires direct import of golang.org/x/sys/unix in cmd/ package\n     2. `os.Readlink(\"/dev/fd/0\")` - simpler but less portable\n     3. Adding a function to pkg/sys - not allowed by task (only cmd/tty/main.go can be created)\n   - Decision not yet finalized, but `unix.Ttyname(0)` is likely the best approach since golang.org/x/sys is already a module dependency\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - One massive task specification message containing: role definition, repository file listing, project context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, source code, requirement states), execution constitution, go style constitution, task description with requirements/design decisions/acceptance criteria, shared protocols, and package contracts.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/tty/main.go` implementing srd052-tty R1.1-R2.1\n   - Verify compilation with `go build -o bin/tty ./cmd/tty/`\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/tty/...`\n   - Verify all acceptance criteria (AC1-AC4)\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the SRD file (`docs/specs/software-requirements/srd052-tty.yaml`) and was about to write the implementation file `cmd/tty/main.go`. No code has been written yet. The SRD reading confirmed the exact requirements:\n   - R1.1: Terminal stdin → print device name, exit 0\n   - R1.2: Non-terminal stdin → print \"not a tty\", exit 1  \n   - R1.3: `-s`/`--silent`/`--quiet` flag → suppress output, exit code only\n   - R2.1: Extra operands → error to stderr, exit 2\n   - R2.2: Unknown flags → error to stderr, exit 2\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write `cmd/tty/main.go` with the complete implementation. The file needs:\n   - SPDX copyright header\n   - Package main with flag parsing for -s/--silent/--quiet\n   - `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` call\n   - Terminal detection using `sys.IsTerminal(os.Stdin.Fd())`\n   - Terminal name retrieval (likely via `golang.org/x/sys/unix.Ttyname(0)`)\n   - Proper exit codes (0, 1, 2)\n   - Error handling for extra operands and unknown flags\n   Then build and vet to verify compilation.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5232/9d2a91a5-010d-4daf-9a7c-2bdc0b52078a.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9d2a91a5-010d-4daf-9a7c-2bdc0b52078a","uuid":"3f4c60b6-ac75-433d-8b73-63815f31f7fa","timestamp":"2026-05-15T00:23:58.454Z","isSynthetic":true}
