{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RcaqHWMoTKGbnfLvL2tKZR","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I have all the information you need. Here's my analysis:\n\n## 1. Functions Exported from pkg/sys/\n\n### terminal.go\nLocated at `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5232/pkg/sys/terminal.go`\n\nExported functions:\n- **`IsTerminal(fd uintptr) bool`** - Checks if a file descriptor is connected to a terminal by attempting to get the window size. Returns true if successful, false on error.\n- **`TerminalWidth() (int, error)`** - Retrieves the width of the terminal by calling `unix.IoctlGetWinsize` on stdout, returning the column count.\n\n### sigpipe.go\nLocated at `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5232/pkg/sys/sigpipe.go`\n\nExported function:\n- **`InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`** - Installs a SIGPIPE handler that listens for SIGPIPE signals and exits with code 0 when received. This matches GNU coreutils behavior. The function uses `signal.Notify` with a buffered channel and is safe to call multiple times (each invocation starts one goroutine).\n\n## 2. Flag Parsing Example - cmd/pwd/main.go\n\nLocated at `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5232/cmd/pwd/main.go`\n\nThe pwd utility demonstrates a manual flag parsing approach:\n\n- **No external flag library** - The code uses custom parsing with `parseArgs(os.Args[1:])` that returns a mode string\n- **Short and long options** - Handles both `-P`/`-L` (short) and `--physical`/`--logical` (long) flags\n- **Special handling** - Includes `--help`, `--version`, and `--` (end of options) support\n- **Error handling** - Validates flags and provides helpful error messages to stderr\n- **Flag precedence** - The last flag wins (later flags override earlier ones)\n- **Helper functions** - `parseShortFlags()` handles bundled short flags like `-LP`\n\nThe pattern is straightforward: loop through args, match against patterns, and exit early for help/version.\n\n## 3. golang.org/x/sys/unix in go.mod\n\n**YES, it's already in go.mod:**\n\nLocated at `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5232/go.mod`\n\n```\nrequire golang.org/x/sys v0.44.0\n```\n\nThe dependency is already present and pinned to version 0.44.0."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9d2a91a5-010d-4daf-9a7c-2bdc0b52078a","uuid":"1be401b6-f15b-4644-aa77-5d2117312606","timestamp":"2026-05-15T00:24:19.642Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need to understand:\n1. What functions are exported from pkg/sys/, especially IsTerminal and InstallSIGPIPEHandler. Read pkg/sys/terminal.go and pkg/sys/sigpipe.go.\n2. How an existing simple cmd/ utility handles flag parsing - read cmd/pwd/main.go as an example (it was recently implemented).\n3. Check if golang.org/x/sys/unix is already in go.mod.\n\nSearch breadth: medium","agentId":"a546b0fbd09070b9c","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I have all the information you need. Here's my analysis:\n\n## 1. Functions Exported from pkg/sys/\n\n### terminal.go\nLocated at `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5232/pkg/sys/terminal.go`\n\nExported functions:\n- **`IsTerminal(fd uintptr) bool`** - Checks if a file descriptor is connected to a terminal by attempting to get the window size. Returns true if successful, false on error.\n- **`TerminalWidth() (int, error)`** - Retrieves the width of the terminal by calling `unix.IoctlGetWinsize` on stdout, returning the column count.\n\n### sigpipe.go\nLocated at `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5232/pkg/sys/sigpipe.go`\n\nExported function:\n- **`InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`** - Installs a SIGPIPE handler that listens for SIGPIPE signals and exits with code 0 when received. This matches GNU coreutils behavior. The function uses `signal.Notify` with a buffered channel and is safe to call multiple times (each invocation starts one goroutine).\n\n## 2. Flag Parsing Example - cmd/pwd/main.go\n\nLocated at `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5232/cmd/pwd/main.go`\n\nThe pwd utility demonstrates a manual flag parsing approach:\n\n- **No external flag library** - The code uses custom parsing with `parseArgs(os.Args[1:])` that returns a mode string\n- **Short and long options** - Handles both `-P`/`-L` (short) and `--physical`/`--logical` (long) flags\n- **Special handling** - Includes `--help`, `--version`, and `--` (end of options) support\n- **Error handling** - Validates flags and provides helpful error messages to stderr\n- **Flag precedence** - The last flag wins (later flags override earlier ones)\n- **Helper functions** - `parseShortFlags()` handles bundled short flags like `-LP`\n\nThe pattern is straightforward: loop through args, match against patterns, and exit early for help/version.\n\n## 3. golang.org/x/sys/unix in go.mod\n\n**YES, it's already in go.mod:**\n\nLocated at `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5232/go.mod`\n\n```\nrequire golang.org/x/sys v0.44.0\n```\n\nThe dependency is already present and pinned to version 0.44.0."}],"totalDurationMs":13406,"totalTokens":21174,"totalToolUseCount":5,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2852,"cache_read_input_tokens":17594,"output_tokens":722,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2852},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":722,"cache_read_input_tokens":17594,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2852,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2852,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{