k(\"/dev/fd/0\")`? On macOS, the `/dev/fd/` entries might support readlink, but testing shows that `/dev/fd/0` isn't a symlink there, so that won't work. I could try using `os.Stat(\"/dev/fd/0\")` and comparing it with entries in `/dev/`, which is what the C `ttyname()` does internally, but that's slow. What if I just use the numeric syscall value directly instead of the deprecated constant? I could hardcode the syscall number for `fcntl` on macOS, though I'm not sure if `unix.Syscall` itself has any issues with this approach. I'm considering using CGo to call the system's ttyname function directly through libSystem, which would be the proper approach on macOS but adds compilation overhead and a dependency that isn't used elsewhere in the project. Let me check if the unix package has a darwin-specific wrapper I might have missed.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":383,"cache_read_input_tokens":45853,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":383},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9d2a91a5-010d-4daf-9a7c-2bdc0b52078a","uuid":"d965321e-8cf9-4251-9601-3cba2b6bd323"}
